rmc-onboarding-window-title = A.R.E.S. Onboarding
rmc-onboarding-window-body = Select a training module
rmc-onboarding-window-close = Close
rmc-onboarding-window-start = Start module
rmc-onboarding-window-replay = Replay module
rmc-onboarding-status-available = Available
rmc-onboarding-status-completed = Completed — available to replay
rmc-onboarding-status-development = In development
rmc-onboarding-lobby-button = Training

rmc-onboarding-task-window-title = Current training task
rmc-onboarding-task-progress = Step {$step} of {$count}
rmc-onboarding-task-exit = Leave training
rmc-onboarding-hint-move = Use your configured movement controls.
rmc-onboarding-hint-interact = Use normal hand interaction on the highlighted object.
rmc-onboarding-hint-pick-up = Click the highlighted item with an empty active hand.
rmc-onboarding-hint-use-in-hand = Use the item in your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-hint-drop = Drop the held item or move it out of your hand.
rmc-onboarding-hint-combat = Use your configured combat-mode action.
rmc-onboarding-hint-approach-food = Walk up to the food vendor behind you.
rmc-onboarding-hint-take-food = Left-click the vendor and take some food.
rmc-onboarding-hint-switch-hands = Press X twice to switch active hands twice.
rmc-onboarding-hint-first-bite = Press Z to use the food in your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-hint-finish-food = Keep eating until the food is gone.
rmc-onboarding-hint-say-nearby = Say something in Nearby chat.
rmc-onboarding-hint-say-looc = Switch to LOOC and send a message.

rmc-onboarding-step-approach-food-title = Hunger and thirst
rmc-onboarding-step-approach-food-1 = Welcome. After waking up, you are usually hungry and thirsty. That is always a good place to start.
rmc-onboarding-step-approach-food-2 = A food vendor is standing behind you.
rmc-onboarding-step-approach-food-3 = I hope I do not need to explain how to walk over to it?
rmc-onboarding-step-approach-food-complete = Excellent. Point at the vendor and press the left mouse button.

rmc-onboarding-step-take-food-title = Getting food
rmc-onboarding-step-take-food-1 = The vendor menu will open.
rmc-onboarding-step-take-food-2 = Choose any food.
rmc-onboarding-step-take-food-complete = Couldn't be better.

rmc-onboarding-step-switch-hands-title = Active hand
rmc-onboarding-step-switch-hands-1 = Look at the bottom of the screen. You have two hands, and your food is probably in the active one.
rmc-onboarding-step-switch-hands-2 = Press X to switch hands. Switch hands twice.
rmc-onboarding-step-switch-hands-complete = Good. The most frequently asked question is solved.

rmc-onboarding-step-first-bite-title = Using an item
rmc-onboarding-step-first-bite-1 = Many items can be interacted with by using the item held in your hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-first-bite-2 = Press Z to use the food in your active hand and take a bite.
rmc-onboarding-step-first-bite-complete = Excellent. Repeat that until your character finishes eating.

rmc-onboarding-step-finish-food-title = Eating
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-food-1 = Keep using the food in your active hand until it is gone.
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-food-complete = Excellent. Your hunger and thirst are gone, and your health has been restored.

rmc-onboarding-step-say-nearby-title = Nearby chat
rmc-onboarding-step-say-nearby-1 = Let us cover chat. The game chat is on your right; characters and players communicate through it.
rmc-onboarding-step-say-nearby-2 = The main channel is Nearby. Every character close to you can hear it.
rmc-onboarding-step-say-nearby-3 = Try saying something.
rmc-onboarding-step-say-nearby-complete = Excellent.

rmc-onboarding-step-say-looc-title = LOOC chat
rmc-onboarding-step-say-looc-1 = There are several chat types. For now, remember LOOC: you can ask the questions you are sure to have there, and experienced players can help.
rmc-onboarding-step-say-looc-2 = Switch to LOOC and say something there.
rmc-onboarding-step-say-looc-complete = Incredible. You have mastered the first steps of this wonderful game. I recommend completing more training sessions; an exciting journey awaits you.

rmc-onboarding-track-full-newbie = Game basics for a new player
rmc-onboarding-track-full-newbie-desc = For players new to SS14, CMU, or RMC. Duration: roughly 10-20 minutes.
rmc-onboarding-track-ss14-veteran = I have played SS14
rmc-onboarding-track-ss14-veteran-desc = A shorter route about CMU/RMC pacing, structure, and expectations.
rmc-onboarding-track-engineering = Engineering
rmc-onboarding-track-engineering-desc = Basics of the engineering corner, tools, lighting, and field support.
rmc-onboarding-track-medical = Medical
rmc-onboarding-track-medical-desc = Practical first aid: casualty evacuation, examination, bleeding control, medicine, and CPR.
rmc-onboarding-track-command = Command
rmc-onboarding-track-command-desc = Basics of command consoles, communication, and order discipline.
rmc-onboarding-track-unknown = Unknown route
rmc-onboarding-track-unknown-desc = Unknown onboarding route.

rmc-onboarding-selected = Selected route: {$track}. Stay inside the training sector and follow the instructions.
rmc-onboarding-declined = Onboarding skipped.
rmc-onboarding-spawn-failed = Failed to create the training map.
rmc-onboarding-already-active = You already have an active training session.
rmc-onboarding-lobby-only = Training can only be started from the lobby.
rmc-onboarding-capacity = All training instances are currently occupied. Please try again shortly.
rmc-onboarding-objective-replaced = The required training object was lost. Rebuilding this step.
rmc-onboarding-map-name = A.R.E.S. onboarding — {$track}
rmc-onboarding-grid-name = A.R.E.S. training deck — {$track}
rmc-onboarding-object-ares = A.R.E.S.
rmc-onboarding-object-ares-interface = A.R.E.S. training interface
rmc-onboarding-object-crowbar = training crowbar
rmc-onboarding-object-supply-crate = field supply crate
rmc-onboarding-object-medical-bed = medical training bed
rmc-onboarding-object-engineering-rack = engineering training rack
rmc-onboarding-object-command-console = command training console
rmc-onboarding-action-ready = Perform the instructed action when you are ready.
rmc-onboarding-complete = Route "{$track}" complete. Initial training data recorded.

rmc-onboarding-step-move-title = Orientation
rmc-onboarding-step-move-1 = Welcome to the training sector. I am A.R.E.S., your automated instruction system.
rmc-onboarding-step-move-2 = This is not an exam. It is a safe deck where mistakes are expected.
rmc-onboarding-step-move-3 = First, feel your character: one step, stop, then another. Do not rush to the props.
rmc-onboarding-step-move-4 = Walk a few tiles along the central lane.
rmc-onboarding-step-move-complete = Movement registered. Coordination is sufficient to continue.

rmc-onboarding-step-console-title = Speaking With A.R.E.S.
rmc-onboarding-step-console-1 = My training terminal is in the center. World objects often carry context without opening a separate lesson panel.
rmc-onboarding-step-console-2 = In CMU/RMC, the environment matters: consoles, lockers, crates, and beds can all be part of a task.
rmc-onboarding-step-console-3 = When in doubt, use normal hand interaction. It is safer than accidental aggressive actions.
rmc-onboarding-step-console-4 = Approach the A.R.E.S. terminal and interact with it by hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-console-complete = Link confirmed. You can address world objects.

rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-title = Items
rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-1 = A training crowbar is on the floor. It is an item, not decoration.
rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-2 = Hands matter. What is in your active hand is usually what you apply.
rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-3 = Do not collect everything during a real round. Understand why you need an item first.
rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-4 = Pick up any training tool from the floor.
rmc-onboarding-step-pickup-complete = Item picked up. Your inventory is now working with you.

rmc-onboarding-step-use-title = Active Hand
rmc-onboarding-step-use-1 = You are holding an item. Many items have an in-hand use action.
rmc-onboarding-step-use-2 = This is different from striking a target. In-hand use usually checks, toggles, or prepares the item.
rmc-onboarding-step-use-3 = In combat and medicine, confusing "use" with "hit" is expensive.
rmc-onboarding-step-use-4 = Use the item in your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-use-complete = In-hand use registered. You distinguish item use from world interaction.

rmc-onboarding-step-drop-title = Free Hands
rmc-onboarding-step-drop-1 = Free hands save time. Sometimes freeing a hand matters more than organizing neatly.
rmc-onboarding-step-drop-2 = If you carry extra clutter, you react slower to orders, treatment, and danger.
rmc-onboarding-step-drop-3 = There is no penalty for mess here. On a real ship, other people will make enough of it.
rmc-onboarding-step-drop-4 = Drop or remove the item from your hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-drop-complete = Hand freed. Good habit for every role.

rmc-onboarding-step-supply-title = Supply
rmc-onboarding-step-supply-1 = A small supply corner is to the right. Boxes and crates decide whether a squad is ready.
rmc-onboarding-step-supply-2 = Supply is not magic. Someone has to take, carry, open, and distribute what is needed.
rmc-onboarding-step-supply-3 = Rations, batteries, lights, and tools look modest but keep the operation moving.
rmc-onboarding-step-supply-4 = Approach the field supply crate and interact with it.
rmc-onboarding-step-supply-complete = Supply point registered. You found a useful prep point, not scenery.

rmc-onboarding-step-combat-title = Combat Mode
rmc-onboarding-step-combat-1 = Combat mode changes intent. Turn it on when you are actually ready for conflict.
rmc-onboarding-step-combat-2 = New players often forget to turn it off and accidentally interfere with allies.
rmc-onboarding-step-combat-3 = In CMU/RMC, discipline near other players matters as much as aim.
rmc-onboarding-step-combat-4 = Toggle combat mode on.
rmc-onboarding-step-combat-complete = Combat mode enabled. Remember: turn it on deliberately and turn it off deliberately.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-title = Medical Corner
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-1 = The medical corner is on the left. It does not replace a medic, but it shows triage logic.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-2 = Do not drag wounded people randomly. Safety first, then delivery to people with medical tools.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-3 = The bed and lockers are visually distinct so you can find them under stress.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-4 = Approach the medical bed and interact with it.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-complete = Medical zone recognized. You know where to look when injuries happen.

rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-title = Engineering Corner
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-1 = The engineering corner is down-right. It has tools, a rack, and lighting supplies.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-2 = Field engineering often starts with access, light, and clear paths.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-3 = Do not take engineering tools without a reason. A missing tool costs a technician minutes.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-4 = Approach the engineering rack and interact with it.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-complete = Engineering zone registered. You can identify a useful work corner.

rmc-onboarding-step-command-title = Command
rmc-onboarding-step-command-1 = The command desk is up top. Command in CMU/RMC runs on information and clear orders.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-2 = A good order is short, possible, and tied to the situation. A bad one sounds impressive and helps no one.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-3 = Even if you are not command, listening to the plan reduces chaos.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-4 = Approach the command console and interact with it.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-complete = Command point confirmed. You know where to look for structure.

rmc-onboarding-step-finish-title = Completion
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-1 = You have covered movement, items, hands, supply, combat, medical, engineering, and command.
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-2 = This does not make you a veteran. It makes your first ten minutes less blind.
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-3 = If you make a mistake on the server, say so and ask. Silence causes more trouble than inexperience.
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-4 = Interact with the A.R.E.S. terminal to finish onboarding.
rmc-onboarding-step-finish-complete = Final confirmation accepted.

rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-move-title = Quick Orientation
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-move-1 = You know SS14, so I will not explain every key.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-move-2 = Walk a few steps to confirm control on the training deck.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-move-complete = Controls confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-console-title = CMU/RMC Differences
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-console-1 = CMU/RMC is faster and harsher than a normal station: less domestic chaos, more field objective.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-console-2 = Watch orders, logistics, and your squad location.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-console-3 = Interact with the A.R.E.S. terminal.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-console-complete = Context accepted.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-supply-title = Gear
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-supply-1 = Gear is not infinite here. Lost supplies return as someone else's problem.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-supply-2 = Learn where boxes and crates are before asking for help.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-supply-3 = Check the field supply crate.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-supply-complete = Supply registered.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-combat-title = Combat Mode
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-combat-1 = Keep combat mode deliberate. Accidental hits on allies damage the operation quickly.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-combat-2 = Toggle combat mode on for the check.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-combat-3 = Remember to turn it off in a live round.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-combat-complete = Combat mode confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-command-title = Orders
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-command-1 = Coordination matters more than personal improvisation here.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-command-2 = If an order is unclear, ask briefly. If the situation changes, report concisely.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-command-3 = Interact with the command console.
rmc-onboarding-step-veteran-command-complete = Short route complete.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-title = Medical Orientation
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-1 = The medical route focuses on recognizing the area and basic discipline.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-2 = Walk a few steps toward the medical corner on the left.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-complete = Movement confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-title = Medical Point
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-1 = A medic works faster when the patient is delivered to a clear location.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-2 = Do not block beds, lockers, or walkways.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-3 = Do not take medical gear without a role or reason.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-4 = Interact with the medical bed.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-station-complete = Medical point confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tool-title = Medical Items
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tool-1 = Any item in hand changes how you interact with a patient.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tool-2 = Pick up a training item and pay attention to the active hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tool-3 = In a real round, confirm what you are about to apply.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tool-complete = Item handling confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-finish-title = Medical Complete
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-finish-1 = Medical discipline: do not block, deliver patients, communicate.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-finish-2 = If you do not know a medicine or procedure, ask before using it.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-finish-3 = Interact with the A.R.E.S. terminal.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-finish-complete = Medical route complete.

rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-move-title = Engineering Orientation
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-move-1 = The engineering route shows the work area and basic tool responsibility.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-move-2 = Walk a few steps toward the engineering corner on the right.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-move-complete = Movement confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-title = Engineering Point
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-1 = Engineering work often begins with a path, light, and access.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-2 = Return tools where a technician can find them.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-3 = Do not dismantle the environment without a reason.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-4 = Interact with the engineering rack.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-station-complete = Engineering point confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-tool-title = Tools
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-tool-1 = Pick up a training tool and check your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-tool-2 = A tool without a task is dangerous to the operation's tempo.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-tool-3 = Ask first if you are unsure in a real round.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-tool-complete = Tool handling confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-finish-title = Engineering Complete
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-finish-1 = Engineering discipline: light, access, repair, order.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-finish-2 = A good technician makes the next path clearer for everyone else.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-finish-3 = Interact with the A.R.E.S. terminal.
rmc-onboarding-step-engineering-finish-complete = Engineering route complete.

rmc-onboarding-step-command-move-title = Command Orientation
rmc-onboarding-step-command-move-1 = The command route focuses on communication and clear orders.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-move-2 = Walk a few steps toward the command desk up top.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-move-complete = Movement confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-title = Command Point
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-1 = Command should not guess. It should receive brief and useful reports.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-2 = An order should answer: who, where, why.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-3 = Do not argue at length during a critical moment. Clarify and act.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-4 = Interact with the command console.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-station-complete = Command point confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-combat-title = Intent Control
rmc-onboarding-step-command-combat-1 = A leader with combat mode on near allies sets a bad example.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-combat-2 = Toggle combat mode on for the check.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-combat-3 = Discipline starts with small habits.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-combat-complete = Intent control confirmed.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-finish-title = Command Complete
rmc-onboarding-step-command-finish-1 = Good command reduces noise and makes the next step obvious.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-finish-2 = Report briefly, listen to the objective, and do not lose people in details.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-finish-3 = Interact with the A.R.E.S. terminal.
rmc-onboarding-step-command-finish-complete = Command route complete.
rmc-onboarding-track-military-equipment = Military equipment, weapons, and grenades
rmc-onboarding-track-military-equipment-desc = Practical training in gearing up, reloading, shooting, weapon attachments, and hand grenades.

rmc-onboarding-hint-insert-magazine = Insert a compatible magazine into any weapon.
rmc-onboarding-hint-kill-drone = Wield a weapon with both hands and kill the xeno drone.
rmc-onboarding-hint-attach-sling = Attach a two-point sling to any compatible weapon.
rmc-onboarding-hint-drop-slung-weapon = Hold the slung weapon and try to drop it.
rmc-onboarding-hint-pick-up-grenade = Pick up the issued grenade from the floor.
rmc-onboarding-hint-kill-grenade-targets = Prime the grenade with Z and throw it at the targets with Ctrl+Q.
rmc-onboarding-hint-listen = Listen to the instructor.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-uniform-title = Basic uniform
rmc-onboarding-step-military-uniform-1 = Most game modes involve combat. If you become a fighter, you should know how to equip yourself.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-uniform-2 = A minimal set of clothing is behind you. Say something when you are dressed.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-uniform-complete = You look like a monkey before a space flight. Just kidding.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-title = Military vendors
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-1 = You did not expect that to be everything, did you?
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-2 = These are the three main vendors used by military personnel.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-3 = Later, you will learn how to select the right equipment for each mission.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-4 = For now, take anything you want.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-5 = Make sure you have a weapon, clothing, body armor, a helmet, and matching magazines.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-6 = Say something in chat when you are done looking around.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-vendors-complete = Body armor is an essential part of a fighter's protection. Different models cover different body parts, but even the smallest protects at least the chest.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-title = Weapons and magazines
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-1 = Armor can also slow you down. Some models are extremely heavy, while others have almost no effect on movement.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-2 = Let us move on to weapons.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-3 = As you may have noticed, every weapon requires its own magazines.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-4 = Insert a compatible magazine into any weapon.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-5 = If one is already loaded, using another magazine on the rifle instantly swaps them.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-magazine-complete = Lovely. Timely magazine changes matter in combat. An enemy may appear when you do not have enough rounds left to stop them.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-drone-title = Shooting
rmc-onboarding-step-military-drone-1 = Time to shoot. Kill the drone target. Remember to wield your weapon with both hands by pressing Z while it is in your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-drone-complete = Well done.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-sling-title = Weapon attachments
rmc-onboarding-step-military-sling-1 = Attachments can change a weapon's characteristics or add entirely new features.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-sling-2 = The weapons vendor stocks a two-point sling. It keeps a dropped weapon from hitting the floor and hangs it from your back instead.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-sling-3 = Attach a two-point sling to any compatible weapon.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-sling-complete = Excellent.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-drop-sling-title = Testing the sling
rmc-onboarding-step-military-drop-sling-1 = Take the weapon in your hands and try to drop it.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-drop-sling-complete = See? The weapon is now hanging from your back.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-pickup-title = Hand grenades
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-pickup-1 = Grenades are usually obtained from requisitions, along with launchers, attachments, and other equipment.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-pickup-2 = Pick up the grenade I placed beneath your feet into your active hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-pickup-complete = Excellent.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-throw-title = Throwing a grenade
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-throw-1 = Press Z with the grenade in your active hand to prime it. Ctrl+Q throws it toward your mouse cursor.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-throw-2 = Aim at the group of Colonial Liberation Front radicals and throw the grenade at them.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-throw-complete = Fine. I thought that would take longer.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-grenade-retry = Bad. Try again.

rmc-onboarding-step-military-finish-title = Completion
rmc-onboarding-step-military-finish-1 = The game has many grenade types: fragmentation, high explosive, and incendiary. You will try them all eventually.
rmc-onboarding-step-military-finish-complete = Excellent. The short course on military equipment, weapons, and grenades is complete.

rmc-onboarding-hint-move-medical-patient = Drag the wounded machine gunner to the center of the room.
rmc-onboarding-hint-examine-medical-patient = Examine the machine gunner with Shift + left click.
rmc-onboarding-hint-treat-bleed = Unpack hemostatic gauze with Z and apply it to the machine gunner.
rmc-onboarding-hint-give-tramadol = Feed the machine gunner one tramadol pill.
rmc-onboarding-hint-give-tricordrazine = Feed the machine gunner one tricordrazine pill.
rmc-onboarding-hint-perform-cpr = Perform CPR three times in a row while respecting the delay between attempts.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-title = Evacuating a casualty
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-1 = It is time to teach you first aid.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-2 = We will begin by helping others.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-3 = A wounded machine gunner is below you, behind the wall.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-4 = Drag him to a safe place: the spot where you are standing now.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-move-patient-complete = Excellent. Now we can begin learning the basics of first aid.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-examine-title = Examining the casualty
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-examine-1 = First, you need to learn what you are dealing with. In other words, find out what happened to the casualty.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-examine-2 = Examine the machine gunner by pressing Shift + left click on him.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-examine-complete = Excellent. As you can see, he clearly has two bleeding wounds.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-bleed-title = First bleeding wound
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-bleed-1 = Bleeding must be stopped first.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-bleed-2 = You have an IFAK pouch containing hemostatic gauze.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-bleed-3 = Take it in hand and unpack it with Z. Then click the wounded machine gunner with the gauze.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-bleed-complete = Excellent. One application closed one wound.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-second-bleed-title = Second bleeding wound
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-second-bleed-1 = There were two bleeding wounds. Close the other one by applying the gauze again.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-second-bleed-complete = Excellent. He is a little safer now.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tramadol-title = Pain relief
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tramadol-1 = Now relieve his pain. Your IFAK contains tramadol, a medium-strength painkiller. Feed one pill to the machine gunner by clicking him with it in hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tramadol-complete = Good. Remember that pills do not act instantly; they need a short time to take effect.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tricordrazine-title = Recovery
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tricordrazine-1 = Now speed up his recovery. Take one tricordrazine pill from your IFAK and feed it to the machine gunner.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-tricordrazine-complete = Excellent. Tricordrazine is a weak general-purpose medicine used to treat damage.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-wrong-pill = That is the wrong pill. You will kill him like that.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-recovery-title = Overdose
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-recovery-1 = In combat, do not fill every casualty with pills indiscriminately.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-recovery-2 = Too much of the same medicine in the bloodstream causes an overdose.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-recovery-3 = This poisons the body and greatly delays recovery.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-recovery-complete = You cannot help him with this injury except by bringing him to the medics.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-patient-fracture = Damn, my leg!! I think the bone is broken!!

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-aftercare-title = Severe injuries
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-aftercare-1 = The game contains many injuries, from fractures and internal bleeding to lost limbs and ruptured organs.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-aftercare-2 = Only an experienced doctor who can operate and understands medicines can repair such damage. An ordinary marine cannot treat it alone.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-aftercare-3 = You can still make the doctors' work much easier by providing basic first aid.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-aftercare-complete = Let us move to the next stage.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-title = Cardiopulmonary resuscitation
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-1 = Not every body can be restored. Some rot before help arrives.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-2 = Doctors sometimes cannot finish treatment before a corpse rots and can no longer be revived.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-3 = You can extend the time before that happens with cardiopulmonary resuscitation, or CPR.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-4 = Perform CPR by left-clicking a dead or critically injured body with an empty hand.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-5 = Keep a steady interval. Performing CPR too quickly will not help.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-6 = Here is a body. Perform CPR correctly three times in a row.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-complete = Good. Now you know what to do when someone asks you to perform CPR.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-cpr-retry = Incorrect. You lost the rhythm. Start again.

rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-aid-finish-title = Completion
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-aid-finish-1 = Excellent. The first-aid course is complete.
rmc-onboarding-step-medical-first-aid-finish-complete = Good luck.
